{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>וייטב [and He dealt well].</b> The proponents of the yod in the first [person] form: sometimes the yod stands, as in this one, and sometimes they replace it with vav, as in \"וְיוֹשֵׁב שָׁם רְעָבִים\" (Psalms 107:36), which is from the root ישב just as וייטב is from יטב. And this good is what is mentioned afterward: \"וַיַּעַשׂ לָהֶם בָּתִּים [and He made them houses]\" — as in \"כִּי־בַיִת יַעֲשֶׂה־לְּךָ ד׳ [for HaShem will make you a house]\" (2 Samuel 7:11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:36.105117698Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}